---
import Legal from '@/layouts/Legal.astro';
import { site } from '@/config/site';
const email = site.contact.email;
---

<Legal title="Privacy policy" description={`How ${site.name} collects, uses and protects personal information.`} lines={['Privacy', '*policy.*']}>
  <p>
    This policy explains how {site.legal.entityName} (“we”, “us”) handles personal information when you visit this
    website or contact us. We collect as little as we need and use it only for the reasons described here.
  </p>

  <h2>What we collect</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Information you send us.</strong> When you use the project enquiry form or email us, we receive the
      details you choose to provide — typically your name, email address, company, phone number and information about
      your project.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Technical information.</strong> Like most websites, our hosting provider may record standard server logs
      (such as IP address, browser type and pages requested) to keep the site secure and working.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How we use it</h2>
  <p>
    We use enquiry details to reply to you, discuss your project and prepare proposals. We do not sell your information
    or use it for unrelated marketing without your permission.
  </p>

  <h2>Form processing</h2>
  <p>
    Enquiries submitted through the website form may be delivered to us by a third-party form service acting on our
    behalf. That service processes the information only to deliver it to our inbox.
  </p>

  <h2>Cookies</h2>
  <p>
    This website does not use advertising or tracking cookies. Your browser’s session storage is used only to remember
    that you have already seen the opening animation during a visit.
  </p>

  <h2>Fonts</h2>
  <p>
    Typefaces are served by Google Fonts. When a page loads, your browser requests the font files from Google’s
    servers, which receive your IP address as part of that request.
  </p>

  <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
  <p>
    We keep enquiry correspondence for as long as needed to respond and, where we work together, for as long as
    required for that relationship and our legal obligations.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    Depending on where you live, you may have the right to access, correct or delete the personal information we hold
    about you, or to object to how we use it. To make a request, email <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>We may update this policy from time to time. The date at the top of this page shows when it last changed.</p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>Questions about privacy? Write to <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>.</p>
</Legal>
